t on our discussion area: https://github.com/xunit/xunit/discussions\r\n  \r\n  No\r\n* > Is this a bug with VSTest (aka Visual Studio Test Explorer, `dotnet test`, `dotnet vstest`,\r\n   > or `vstest.console.exe`)? Open those issues here:\r\n  > https://github.com/xunit/visualstudio.xunit/issues/\r\n  \r\n  No\r\n* > Did you search the docs @ https://xunit.net/ ?\r\n\r\nYes. No search result is found so far. Check [here](https://www.google.com/search?q=%22raisesexception%22+site%3Ahttps%3A%2F%2Fxunit.net&sca_esv=586234374&rlz=1C1GCEA_en__1042__1042&sxsrf=AM9HkKn8HI306YQp3csn2z9lDAgu6039ug%3A1701253072974&ei=0A9nZc-DO5-khbIPodCM8Ao&ved=0ahUKEwjPq9nI_eiCAxUfUkEAHSEoA64Q4dUDCBA&uact=5&oq=%22raisesexception%22+site%3Ahttps%3A%2F%2Fxunit.net&gs_lp=Egxnd3Mtd2l6LXNlcnAiKCJyYWlzZXNleGNlcHRpb24iIHNpdGU6aHR0cHM6Ly94dW5pdC5uZXRIjjdQwCFYrDVwA3gAkAEAmAFHoAHVB6oBAjE2uAEDyAEA-AEB4gMEGAEgQYgGAQ&sclient=gws-wiz-serp), [here](https://www.google.com/search?q=%22xunit.sdk%22+site%3Ahttps%3A%2F%2Fxunit.net&sca_esv=586234374&rlz=1C1GCEA_en__1042__1042&sxsrf=AM9HkKmBk_IE_ACC42tICEPMDnAbCFFQOQ%3A1701253065705&ei=yQ9nZfvSKsi8hbIPmYm7MA&ved=0ahUKEwi7253F_eiCAxVIXkEAHZnEDgYQ4dUDCBA&uact=5&oq=%22xunit.sdk%22+site%3Ahttps%3A%2F%2Fxunit.net&gs_lp=Egxnd3Mtd2l6LXNlcnAiIiJ4dW5pdC5zZGsiIHNpdGU6aHR0cHM6Ly94dW5pdC5uZXRIxxxQiQdY0BpwAXgAkAEAmAE6oAFtqgEBMrgBA8gBAPgBAeIDBBgBIEGIBgE&sclient=gws-wiz-serp)\r\n\r\n* > Did you search the issues list to see if someone already reported it?\r\n  > When looking for duplicates, make sure to look through open **and** closed issues.\r\n  \r\n Yes. I am the first unluckly victim from the breaking change.\r\n  \r\n* > Did you create a simple repro for the problem?\r\n  > Bugs without repro projects will be automatically closed.\r\n \r\n It is a code snippet, easily reproducible. \r\n \r\n```\r\nvar exception = Assert.IsType<RaisesException>(recorded);\r\nAssert.Equal(WatchdogHelper.NoEventRaisedError, exception.Actual);   // offending line\r\nAssert.Equal(nameof(ServiceConnectionStatusEventArgs), exception.Expected);  // offending line\r\n```\r\n\r\nIn xunit 2.4.2, the `Xunit.Sdk.RaisesException.Actual`, `Xunit.Sdk.RaisesException.Expected` work.\r\n\r\nHowever, in xunit 2.5.0 & onwards, `Actual` & `Expected` properties are missing.\r\nI cannot find any note on those properties from the [xunit 2.5.0 release note](https://xunit.net/releases/v2/2.5.0).\r\n\r\nMy team would like to use the latest version of the xunit library, however due to the breaking change above, we could not do so.\r\n\r\n`RaisesException` inherits from `XunitException` and there had been some work done in `XunitException` constructor (see [here](https://github.com/xunit/xunit/issues/2737))\r\n\r\nCan `Actual` & `Expected` properties be reinstated in `RaisesException` class please?\r\nAppreciate any help & support on this matter.\r\nThanks.\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xunit/xunit/issues/2832/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xunit/xunit/issues/2832/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"not_planned"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]